course: dictionary
lesson: 6931
title: Paddlefish: a fish with a paddle nose
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A paddlefish is a large fish that lives in fresh water, in rivers. Its name is the clue: it has a long, flat snout shaped like a paddle, the kind you use to row a boat. When you meet a new word, look for clues in its own parts as well as in the sentence around it.
explain: «The Chinese paddlefish could grow several metres long.» Several metres means more than a few metres, so this fish was very big, much bigger than most fish you have seen. The sentence gives you the size, and the dictionary gives you the rest: large, freshwater, flat snout.
explain: Some sentences tell you what happened to a creature. «It was declared extinct in 2020» means people officially said there were no more of it left alive. Extinct means gone for good, and it is a sad word to read in a science lesson.
fact: A paddlefish is a large freshwater fish with a long, flat, paddle-shaped snout.
fact: Paddlefish are found in the rivers of the USA.
fact: Paddlefish is a noun, and the plural is also paddlefish: one paddlefish, two paddlefish.
fact: «Extinct» means no longer alive anywhere in the world.
fact: «Dams» are walls built across rivers, and they can block fish from the places where they lay eggs.
exercise: «The paddlefish has a flat snout shaped like a paddle.» What is a paddlefish? | *A large freshwater fish with a paddle-shaped snout | A plant that grows in ponds | A small bird that swims in the sea | A kind of paddle used to row a boat
exercise: «The Chinese paddlefish could grow several metres long.» What does several metres mean? | Exactly one metre | Too small to see | *More than a few metres long | Only a few centimetres
exercise: «The Chinese paddlefish was declared extinct in 2020.» Find and copy one word that means gone for good. | paddlefish | Chinese | 2020 | *extinct
test: «Dams blocked the paddlefish from the places where it laid eggs.» Why could this harm paddlefish? | *It could not reach the places it needed to lay eggs | It grew too fast | It turned into a bird | It became much smaller
test: The dictionary says paddlefish live in the rivers of the USA. Where would you most likely find one? | On a mountain top | In a salty sea, far from land | *In the rivers of the USA
exam: «Nets, electric fishing and dams did the rest, and the giant Chinese paddlefish was lost too.» What does lost mean here? | Found again by scientists | Hidden in the mud, ready to come back | Carried away by the current | *Gone for good, no longer alive
